WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.410
- All right everybody let's wrap.

00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.990
Yeah, I heard it.

00:00:02.990 --> 00:00:05.140
Let's wrap up this hour
with one more story

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:06.140
sure to make you smile,

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:07.141
this is "What I'm Liking."

00:00:07.141 --> 00:00:09.611
(upbeat music)

00:00:09.611 --> 00:00:10.710
(audience cheering)

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:12.820
It takes a crazy amount of hard work

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:15.630
to land a full ride
scholarship for college.

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:17.890
So we should all be impressed

00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:20.010
with 18 year old Josh in
St. Charles, Missouri,

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:22.069
who secured a four year scholarship

00:00:22.069 --> 00:00:24.650
worth $43,000, that's incredible.

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:25.483
(audience cheering)

00:00:25.483 --> 00:00:26.610
Way to go.

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:30.180
But, that's only part of
what makes him remarkable.

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:32.210
Now that he set on his educational path.

00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:34.791
He wants to pay it
forward to other students.

00:00:34.791 --> 00:00:36.050
Incredible.

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:38.480
So he's using the money
he saved up for college

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:41.350
to give out scholarships of his own.

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:42.240
I love him.

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:43.320
His name is Josh.

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:44.540
We have Josh on the line.

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:45.562
Say hi y'all.

00:00:45.562 --> 00:00:47.079
(audience cheering)

00:00:47.079 --> 00:00:48.239
Hi Josh.

00:00:48.239 --> 00:00:49.160
- How you doing?

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:50.300
- Oh my gosh.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:51.350
I want friends like you,

00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:52.340
you're so sweet.

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:53.970
This is the sweetest thing ever

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:56.258
and first of all, congratulations
on your scholarship man.

00:00:56.258 --> 00:00:57.091
That's so cool.

00:00:57.091 --> 00:00:58.339
(audience cheering)

00:00:58.339 --> 00:00:59.820
- Thank you.
- Yeah.

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:02.070
- So what are you studying?

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:04.099
- So I'm actually majoring
in biomedical sciences,

00:01:04.099 --> 00:01:06.660
and I'm as SCMP in their
pre-optometry program

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:08.981
because my plan is to take my
degree in biomedical sciences

00:01:08.981 --> 00:01:11.110
and become an optometrist,

00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:12.490
because being an eye doctor is something

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:15.080
that's kind of interested
me for a long time,

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:16.920
'cause my family has very poor vision.

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:17.840
I wear contacts,

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:18.821
my mom wears contacts,

00:01:18.821 --> 00:01:20.510
my brother wears contacts.

00:01:20.510 --> 00:01:21.790
So I feel like it's just

00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:23.330
a really important field of medicine.

00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:24.491
That's going to be super
valuable in the future.

00:01:24.491 --> 00:01:25.941
(audience cheering)

00:01:25.941 --> 00:01:29.270
- So now you're paying it forward,

00:01:29.270 --> 00:01:30.770
so tell us about your scholarship.

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:32.800
- So yeah, so last year
during my senior year

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:33.633
in high school,

00:01:33.633 --> 00:01:35.260
I decided to start a
scholarship fund called the

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:37.640
Joshua Nelson Leaders
In Action Scholarship.

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:39.580
Basically what encouraged me to start this

00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:40.450
was my faith,

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:41.510
I'm a man of strong faith,

00:01:41.510 --> 00:01:43.830
and I feel like it comes
from the biblical principle

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:45.270
of being of a cheerful giver,

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:46.750
'cause from a young age I've kinda

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:48.600
just been super excited to give back.

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:51.960
And once God opened a
door for me to be able

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:53.170
to give back in a big way,

00:01:53.170 --> 00:01:54.550
then I jumped on it right away.

00:01:54.550 --> 00:01:56.730
So, I decided to take a thousand dollars

00:01:56.730 --> 00:01:58.260
out of my college savings,

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:00.829
and I decided to start
my own scholarship fund.

00:02:00.829 --> 00:02:04.950
And what happened was a
local nonprofit organization

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:06.970
decided to pick up the story.

00:02:06.970 --> 00:02:08.500
Local news station started picking it up

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:10.490
and we got a lot of traction,

00:02:10.490 --> 00:02:12.870
and we were able to raise
$17,000 in scholarships

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:15.380
to where the Joshua Nelson
Leaders in Action Scholarship

00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:17.620
would be funded for over a decade.

00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:18.530
- That's incredible,

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:20.810
you are such a remarkable young man.

00:02:20.810 --> 00:02:22.180
Oh, the future is bright now.

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:24.700
Okay, well thank you so much, Josh.

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:26.477
I'm liking your posts right now, right.

00:02:26.477 --> 00:02:28.210
- [Josh] Alright.

00:02:28.210 --> 00:02:29.440
- Hey my man.

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:32.490
That's not all our season
long partner Pilot Pen,

00:02:32.490 --> 00:02:34.050
the go-to pen at the Kelly Clarkson show

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:37.120
likes to celebrate incredible
people, just like you.

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:39.500
So they're gonna be using
their friction erasable pen

00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:41.730
to write you a cheque
for a thousand dollars.

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:42.917
How's that sound?

00:02:42.917 --> 00:02:44.210
(audience cheering)

00:02:44.210 --> 00:02:45.043
- Awesome.

00:02:45.043 --> 00:02:48.410
- And I hear that it's your goal you know,

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:50.570
to create to where you can have $10,000

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:51.430
to be able to give someone,

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:53.610
so I'm gonna give you $9,000,

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:55.477
and you can make that 10.

00:02:55.477 --> 00:02:56.536
(audience cheering)

00:02:56.536 --> 00:02:59.368
And I'm all about educating people,

00:02:59.368 --> 00:03:01.680
I think what you're doing,

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:03.243
is an amazing thing.

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:05.673
I think.
- [Josh] Thank you so much.

00:03:05.673 --> 00:03:07.220
- People should not have to worry about

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:09.250
the financial part of it because,

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:10.920
you know education is.
- [Josh] Right.

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:12.720
- It brings so much opportunity to people.

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:14.360
So I think it's so
beautiful what you're doing.

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:15.239
Thank you.

00:03:15.239 --> 00:03:16.227
(audience cheering)

00:03:16.227 --> 00:03:17.433
- Thank you so much.

